result: 'together happy-path lowering complete. `dispatch\n body` (anonymous) inside
  together = concurrent scheduler task; named dispatch stays lazy generator. Typer
  renames anon dispatches to unique __anon{id}. MIR Function gained scheduler_task
  flag (shares gen capture ABI but returns normally instead of gen-suspend, fixing
  null-caller-ctx segfault). Lowerer.scope_stack drives lower_together: __scope_create
  -> body -> __scope_stop_actors -> __scope_join. Anon task captures enclosing locals
  (collect_var_refs_block ∩ var_types), passed via gen struct slots; codegen emit_scope_spawn
  creates coro + jinn_scope_register_child + jinn_sched_spawn. Scope-owned actors:
  spawn inside scope calls jinn_actor_spawn_scoped (non-daemon, registered, mailbox
  tracked) so scope auto-stop+drains on exit. uses_concurrency now recurses Together.
  Conformance: scope_joins_all_dispatches, scope_owned_actor_drains_on_exit, daemon_spawn_outside_scope_unchanged
  — all 14 concurrency tests pass, 912 bulk tests pass, zero warnings. (column_* failures
  pre-existing.) Scope cancellation/stop-scope deferred to 2-6-4.'
description: 'Lower hir::Stmt::Together to MIR: emit __scope_create -> scope ptr bound
  in a scope-local var; set current coro''s scope for the body''s dynamic extent (push/pop
  via runtime tl or by passing scope to spawns lexically). Children: dispatch/spawn
  inside body register with the scope. Block end: __scope_stop_actors then __scope_join.
  codegen magic.rs handles __scope_create/__scope_join/__scope_stop_actors/__scope_register.
  Scope name binds to scope ptr; `stop <scopevar>` lowers to scope cancel (distinguish
  ActorRef vs Scope by type). DoD: scope_joins_all_dispatches + scope_owned_actor_drains_on_exit
  + daemon_spawn_outside_scope_unchanged tests pass; all 11 existing concurrency tests
  still pass.'
